1: # Infinity collision: relative circle-quotient excision
2: 
3: This is the complete-map audit draft following IF.1--11 in
4: notes/part3_source_infinity_fourfold_working.md. It retains the actual
5: source, Cartier line, cap and physical circle maps. The original global
6: source-coordinate/root endpoint dictionary remains explicit in IF.1--6.
7: No eight-dimensional signature or unproved spin extension is substituted
8: for the circle-quotient comparison.
9: 
10: ## IE.1. Two actual collision fillings and their boundary families
11: 
12: Choose a small closed source-base disc \(U\) around \(t=0\), disjoint
13: from the selected value and the cap. Its boundary annulus contains no
14: singular source fibre for any small \(\epsilon\). Fix a nonzero
15: reference \(\epsilon_*\). Let \(S_\epsilon\) be the actual minimal
16: source over \(U\), with its marked small resolution at \(\epsilon=0\),
17: and retain \(M_a=\mathcal O(aG-O)\), \(a=1,2\).
18: 
19: The first filling \(W_{\rm c}(N)\) is the regularized collision family
20: IF.8--10, with \(\lambda=\epsilon^N\lambda_0\). After its
21: determinant-one regularization the total fourfold is smooth; the
22: function \(\epsilon\) may have a singular central fibre. Its actual
23: source/line periods are (IF.15), its physical circle is \(\delta\),
24: and its protected boundary is the primitive source-line/parameter
25: chain.
26: 
27: The reference filling \(W_{\rm r}(N)\) uses the fixed source
28: \(S_{\epsilon_*}\), its fixed actual line \(M_a\), and the same scalar
29: \(\lambda=\epsilon^N\lambda_0\). No selected zero lies in \(U\).
30: Its actual suspension lift \(B_0\) is therefore invertible over
31: \(U\), including both ordinary I1 fibres. Use the full chain
32: \[
33:  X_j=V\epsilon^{-j},\qquad
34:  Y_j=\epsilon^{j+1}/V,\qquad X_jY_j=\epsilon ,
35:  \quad j\in\mathbb Z.                                  \tag{IE.1}
